---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config/site';

const consequences = [
  {
    sev: 'hint',
    label: 'Hint',
    what: 'I point it out',
    detail:
      'Most problems are misunderstandings or somebody having a rough day. A clear note is usually enough.'
  },
  {
    sev: 'info',
    label: 'Info',
    what: 'I ask you to stop',
    detail: 'A direct message from me, not a bot. Most problems end here.'
  },
  {
    sev: 'warn',
    label: 'Warning',
    what: 'I remove you from the space',
    detail: 'You lose access to the place where it happened. I will tell you why when I can.'
  },
  {
    sev: 'error',
    label: 'Error',
    what: 'I take it further',
    detail:
      'Threats, stalking, or publishing private information may go to platform moderators or law enforcement.'
  }
];

const lastChanged = new Date(SITE.conductUpdated).toLocaleDateString('en-GB', {
  day: 'numeric',
  month: 'short',
  year: 'numeric'
});
---

<Base
  title="Code of conduct"
  description="How people are expected to treat one another in the spaces Michael runs."
>
  <main id="main">
    <div class="shell read">
      <aside class="rail">
        <dl>
          <div><dt>Applies to</dt><dd>Spaces I run and direct contact</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Enforced by</dt><dd><a href="/about/">Michael Jolley</a></dd></div>
          <div><dt>Last changed</dt><dd>{lastChanged}</dd></div>
        </dl>
      </aside>

      <article data-pagefind-body data-pagefind-filter="kind:page">
        <header class="storyhead">
          <span class="path">conduct</span>
          <h1>
            Be the person you'd want
            <span class="squiggle"><span>reading your worst commit.</span></span>
          </h1>
          <p class="lede">
            This site points to a few places where people build and learn together. Those
            places only work when nobody has to brace for cruelty before joining in.
          </p>
        </header>

        <div class="prose conduct-body">
          <div class="callout">
            <span class="tag">The rule</span>
            <p>
              Treat people like people. Critique the idea, code, or decision without treating
              the person as the problem.
            </p>
          </div>

          <h2>What that looks like in practice</h2>
          <p>
            Be curious before you are certain. Ask about the constraints, explain the tradeoff
            you see, and leave room for context you do not have.
          </p>
          <p>
            Disagreement is welcome. Say what you think, show your work, and let the other
            person make their own call. Winning the exchange is not the goal.
          </p>
          <p>
            Respect names, pronouns, experience, privacy, and boundaries. Give credit when
            somebody else's work helped you.
          </p>

          <h2>What does not belong here</h2>
          <p>
            Harassment, slurs, threats, stalking, intimidation, or unwanted sexual attention.
            Nothing clever to say about these. They are out.
          </p>
          <p>
            Publishing private information about somebody else. That includes addresses,
            phone numbers, private messages, and anything shared in confidence.
          </p>
          <p>
            Sustained disruption. Honest criticism is useful. Following somebody around,
            piling on, or making it impossible for everyone else to participate is not.
          </p>
          <p>
            Spam and disguised advertising. A useful link is fine. Turning every exchange
            into a sales pitch is not.
          </p>

          <h2>Where this applies</h2>
          <p>
            This covers the spaces I control and direct contact connected to them. Behavior
            elsewhere may matter when it creates a real safety problem here.
          </p>

          <h2>What happens when somebody breaks the rule</h2>
          <p>
            There is no committee. It is me. I usually start small, but this is not a promise
            to walk through every step when somebody is in danger.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="crows">
          {
            consequences.map((c) => (
              <div class="crow">
                <span class={`sev sev-${c.sev}`}>{c.label}</span>
                <div>
                  <h3>{c.what}</h3>
                  <p>{c.detail}</p>
                </div>
              </div>
            ))
          }
        </div>

        <div class="prose conduct-tail">
          <h2>If I get it wrong</h2>
          <p>
            <a href={`mailto:${SITE.conductEmail}`}>Email the conduct inbox</a>. I have
            reversed moderation calls before and I will do it again. I will not argue about
            somebody's safety in public.
          </p>

          <h2>If it's about me</h2>
          <p>
            I'm the one who runs this, which makes the conversation awkward. Email the conduct
            inbox anyway. If you do not want me to handle it alone, say so and I will ask
            somebody I trust to read it first.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="hero-actions conduct-acts">
          <a class="btn primary" href={`mailto:${SITE.conductEmail}`}>Email about conduct</a>
          <a class="btn" href="/all/">Browse articles and videos</a>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </main>
</Base>

<style>
  .conduct-body {
    margin-top: 2rem;
  }
  .conduct-tail,
  .conduct-acts {
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
  }
</style>
